    }

    .demo-box {
        border: 1px solid #dee2e6;
        background: #ffffff;
        padding: 20px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        margin: 18px 0;
    }

    .section-demo {
        border: 2px solid #dee2e6;
        padding: 20px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        background: #f8f9fa;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
    }

    .table th {
        background-color: #f8f9fa;
    }
</style>

<main id="main-content" class="container py-5">
    <div class="row g-4">

        <!-- Left Sidebar -->
        <div class="col-lg-3">
            @Html.Partial("~/Areas/HTML/Views/Shared/HTMLTopics.cshtml")
        </div>

        <!-- Main Content -->
        <div class="col-lg-9 content-section">

            <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">HTML Section Element</h1>

            <p>
                The HTML <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> element represents a thematic
                grouping of related content within a web page. It is commonly used
                to divide a document into meaningful parts such as courses, services,
                features, chapters, or topics.
            </p>

            <div class="info-box">
                <strong>Key Point:</strong>
                Use <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> when a group of content forms a
                meaningful topic or part of the document.
            </div>

            <h2>1. What is the section Element?</h2>

            <p>
                The <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> element is a semantic HTML element
                used to group related content around a common theme.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;section&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;HTML Forms&lt;/h2&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;
        Learn how to create HTML forms.
    &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>


<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>
            <h3>Output</h3>

            <div class="demo-box">
                <section class="section-demo">
                    <h3 class="mt-0">HTML Forms</h3>

                    <p class="mb-0">
                        Learn how to create HTML forms.
                    </p>
                </section>
            </div>

            <h2>2. Purpose of the section Element</h2>

            <p>
                A section groups content that belongs together conceptually.
                Each section should represent a meaningful part of the document.
            </p>

            <p>Examples include:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Introduction section</li>
                <li>Course section</li>
                <li>Services section</li>
                <li>Features section</li>
                <li>Testimonials section</li>
                <li>Contact section</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Basic Section Example</h2>

            <pre><code>&lt;section&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;
        We provide technology training programs.
    &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>

            <h2>4. Section with Heading</h2>

            <p>
                A section commonly contains a heading that describes the topic
                of the section.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;section&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;Our Courses&lt;/h2&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;
        Explore our technology courses.
    &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>


<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>
            <div class="info-box">
                A heading makes the purpose of the section easier to understand.
            </div>

            <h2>5. Multiple Sections</h2>

            <p>
                A page can contain multiple sections, each representing a different topic.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;section&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;HTML&lt;/h2&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;
        Learn HTML fundamentals.
    &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;CSS&lt;/h2&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;
        Learn CSS styling.
    &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;JavaScript&lt;/h2&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;
        Learn JavaScript programming.
    &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>


<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>
            <h2>6. Section Inside main</h2>

            <p>
                Sections are commonly placed inside the main content area.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;main&gt;

    &lt;section&gt;

        &lt;h2&gt;HTML Basics&lt;/h2&gt;

        &lt;p&gt;
            Learn the fundamentals of HTML.
        &lt;/p&gt;

    &lt;/section&gt;

    &lt;section&gt;

        &lt;h2&gt;HTML Forms&lt;/h2&gt;

        &lt;p&gt;
            Learn how to create HTML forms.
        &lt;/p&gt;

