        Try It
    </button>
</div>
            <h2>11. Section with ID</h2>

            <p>
                An <code>id</code> can be used to uniquely identify a section,
                especially when another part of the page needs to link to it.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;section id="html-basics"&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;HTML Basics&lt;/h2&gt;

    &lt;p&gt;
        Learn HTML fundamentals.
    &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>


<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>
            <h2>12. Linking to a Section</h2>

            <p>
                A navigation link can point directly to a section using its
                <code>id</code>.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;nav&gt;

    &lt;a href="#html-basics"&gt;
        HTML Basics
    &lt;/a&gt;

    &lt;a href="#html-forms"&gt;
        HTML Forms
    &lt;/a&gt;

&lt;/nav&gt;

&lt;section id="html-basics"&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;HTML Basics&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section id="html-forms"&gt;

    &lt;h2&gt;HTML Forms&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>


<div class="try-it-container">
